All these memories that you're saying that
we have together. I don't...

1342
01:29:24.970 --> 01:29:26.030
I don't have them.

1343
01:29:29.640 --> 01:29:31.862
And I do see why. you
know. she would love

1344
01:29:31.942 --> 01:29:35.520
you. the girl you wrote
that letter to. but...

1345
01:29:38.950 --> 01:29:44.190
I understand that you did what you had to
do to protect her.

1346
01:29:46.430 --> 01:29:48.830
And for that. I'm so grateful.

1347
01:29:52.550 --> 01:29:58.270
But I... I don't love you.

1348
01:30:13.900 --> 01:30:16.440
I should probably go now.

1349
01:30:23.140 --> 01:30:24.200
I really am sorry. Peter.

1350
01:30:43.050 --> 01:30:44.390
I don't have a phone.

1351
01:31:14.230 --> 01:31:15.230
I'm sorry.

1352
01:31:32.720 --> 01:31:39.030
Thank you.

1353
01:31:39.310 --> 01:31:40.310
Yeah. sure.

1354
01:31:41.230 --> 01:31:42.230
I've been a while.

1355
01:31:42.510 --> 01:31:42.810
Oh yeah?

1356
01:31:43.270 --> 01:31:44.270
Yeah. of course.

1357
01:31:53.780 --> 01:31:54.780
Do you want to come up?

1358
01:31:57.220 --> 01:31:59.040
Just to say hi to Ned. maybe?

1359
01:32:02.760 --> 01:32:05.640
I would love that.

1360
01:32:06.580 --> 01:32:07.660
The Hulk. a.k.a.

1361
01:32:07.760 --> 01:32:12.560
Dr. Bruce Banner. is in custody. currently
being transferred to a psychiatric ward.

1362
01:32:12.720 --> 01:32:18.480
After years as a peaceful academic.
the question the world asked today is.

1363
01:32:18.900 --> 01:32:19.900
what finally snapped?

1364
01:32:21.860 --> 01:32:22.860
Huh?

1365
01:32:26.980 --> 01:32:27.980
Hey. I'm nearby.

1366
01:32:28.760 --> 01:32:29.900
Hey. I'm nearby.

1367
01:32:30.060 --> 01:32:30.340
And Dave?

1368
01:32:30.540 --> 01:32:30.700
Yeah.

1369
01:32:31.180 --> 01:32:32.180
Hey. I'm nearby.

1370
01:32:33.740 --> 01:32:35.580
Uh. you're not going to believe this.

1371
01:32:35.920 --> 01:32:40.520
But the Spidey Tracker app says that
Spider-Man is in the direct facility.

1372
01:32:41.220 --> 01:32:41.540
Oh yeah?

1373
01:32:41.780 --> 01:32:42.780
No way. that's crazy.

1374
01:32:43.700 --> 01:32:44.700
Hey. I'm nearby.

1375
01:32:45.700 --> 01:32:46.740
Uh. Ned?

1376
01:32:46.980 --> 01:32:47.420
Spider-Man?

1377
01:32:47.540 --> 01:32:48.020
Spider-Man?

1378
01:32:48.160 --> 01:32:48.300
Ned?

1379
01:32:48.301 --> 01:32:49.720
It's nice to meet you. Ned.

1380
01:32:51.360 --> 01:32:51.800
Hello.

1381
01:32:51.801 --> 01:32:53.400
I'm not. like. a weirdo or anything.

1382
01:32:53.640 --> 01:32:54.640
He's a little weird.

1383
01:32:54.800 --> 01:32:56.820
Why. uh. why are you here?

1384
01:32:57.680 --> 01:33:00.300
Oh. I. uh... I was
on a subway...

1385
01:33:01.040 --> 01:33:02.840
...platform. right. and she was on her
phone.

1386
01:33:03.020 --> 01:33:05.260
Yeah. I got a little distracted and the
train was coming.

1387
01:33:05.340 --> 01:33:06.820
And I just swooped her right up.

1388
01:33:09.640 --> 01:33:11.100
Oh my God.

1389
01:33:12.440 --> 01:33:13.800
Why has that never happened to me?

1390
01:33:14.340 --> 01:33:17.780
So. what if you're mid-swing and you
decide to need to pee?

1391
01:33:18.060 --> 01:33:19.580
Do you just land on top of a building?

1392
01:33:19.700 --> 01:33:19.860
What?

1393
01:33:20.360 --> 01:33:22.656
Do you drop down the ground level and run
into a coffee shop?

1394
01:33:22.680 --> 01:33:24.176
And you're like. you don't spider-man I
need to pee.

1395
01:33:24.200 --> 01:33:25.720
Or do you find a rooftop somewhere?

1396
01:33:26.040 --> 01:33:27.860
No. I don't find a rooftop somewhere.
Ned.

1397
01:33:27.940 --> 01:33:29.956
Is this really what you want to be asking
him right now?

1398
01:33:29.980 --> 01:33:30.640
Yeah. dude. come on.

1399
01:33:30.700 --> 01:33:31.400
You can ask me anything.

1400
01:33:31.540 --> 01:33:32.976
You want to know how my web shooters work?

1401
01:33:33.000 --> 01:33:34.916
I mean. I already know how the web
shooters work.

1402
01:33:34.940 --> 01:33:35.520
Is that right?

1403
01:33:35.860 --> 01:33:39.009
Well. there's obviously
some sort of sheer thinning

1404
01:33:39.010 --> 01:33:41.260
fluid that is cycling
within a chamber. right?

1405
01:33:41.300 --> 01:33:42.360
So you can keep it slippery for them.

1406
01:33:42.361 --> 01:33:44.204
And then when you
activate it by pressing on

1407
01:33:44.205 --> 01:33:46.120
the triggers. it runs
through a Teflon turbine.

1408
01:33:46.520 --> 01:33:49.860
And then. it hardens when it interacts
with the air. right?

1409
01:33:52.640 --> 01:33:57.216
I mean. not exactly. but... Okay. okay.
well then tell me what's in the web fluid.

1410
01:33:57.240 --> 01:34:01.420
I would guess something like a long-chain
polymer nylon.

1411
01:34:01.980 --> 01:34:02.580
It's pretty close.

1412
01:34:02.880 --> 01:34:03.380
Okay. okay.

1413
01:34:03.780 --> 01:34:05.920
What about Nomex or... oh. Kevlar!

1414
01:34:08.180 --> 01:34:10.000
Alright. then keep those secrets.

1415
01:34:10.001 --> 01:34:14.180
If you are very good at the incident with
the dragon. I was barely involved.

1416
01:34:14.900 --> 01:34:18.260
All I did was simply give your uncle and
his little nudge out the door.

1417
01:34:20.720 --> 01:34:21.720
Solid reference.

1418
01:34:23.160 --> 01:34:24.360
Ooh. bondme time!

1419
01:34:24.800 --> 01:34:25.800
You ordered bondmes?

1420
01:34:26.160 --> 01:34:27.220
I ordered five bondmes.

1421
01:34:27.420 --> 01:34:28.516
We have Spider-Man in the apartment.

1422
01:34:28.540 --> 01:34:29.540
He's gonna get fat.

1423
01:34:32.740 --> 01:34:33.680
Sorry about him.

1424
01:34:33.681 --> 01:34:35.521
He's just. like. very excited that you're
here.

1425
01:34:35.760 --> 01:34:36.260
Are you kidding?

1426
01:34:36.340 --> 01:34:37.900
This is. like. the most fun I've had in
years.

1427
01:34:37.901 --> 01:34:39.760
I really miss you guys.

1428
01:34:41.820 --> 01:34:43.640
You guys really do look like best friends.

1429
01:34:44.180 --> 01:34:45.180
What do you mean?

1430
01:34:54.180 --> 01:34:55.560
You should tell him.

1431
01:34:56.160 --> 01:34:57.160
He can handle it.

1432
01:34:58.900 --> 01:34:59.900
Yeah. I know.

1433
01:35:06.680 --> 01:35:15.020
When she was inhabiting you on the rooftop.
she kissed me. and I kissed her back.

1434
01:35:15.400 --> 01:35:17.680
Because I thought it was you. but I didn't
know.

1435
01:35:18.320 --> 01:35:20.020
And I'm really sorry.

1436
01:35:21.460 --> 01:35:22.700
I just thought you should know.

1437
01:35:25.060 --> 01:35:26.060
Thanks for telling me.

1438
01:35:29.570 --> 01:35:32.430
I mean. it's not like I remember anything
anyway. so...

1439
01:35:33.870 --> 01:35:34.270
Really?

1440
01:35:34.870 --> 01:35:35.270
Yeah.

1441
01:35:35.670 --> 01:35:36.050
It was weird.

1442
01:35:36.190 --> 01:35:37.790
It was. like. one second
I was sitting at my desk.

1443
01:35:37.791 --> 01:35:40.051
and the next second I
was lying on the street.

1444
01:35:40.430 --> 01:35:42.150
I don't know. like. a light switch went
off.

1445
01:35:44.750 --> 01:35:45.150
What?

1446
01:35:45.750 --> 01:35:47.010
So you don't remember anything?

1447
01:35:49.430 --> 01:35:50.430
No. why?

1448
01:35:51.010 --> 01:35:54.230
Metzger said he remembered thinking about
someone named Sarah. but what you're

1449
01:35:54.231 --> 01:35:56.730
saying is that you don't remember anything
at all.

1450
01:35:59.250 --> 01:36:01.190
I mean. yeah. it was instantaneous.

1451
01:36:01.650 --> 01:36:02.810
That's what made it so scary.

1452
01:36:04.870 --> 01:36:05.930
He lied to me.

1453
01:36:09.050 --> 01:36:10.670
I heard you called Leshy.

1454
01:36:11.010 --> 01:36:12.150
Yeah. my name's Jean Grey.

1455
01:36:12.350 --> 01:36:14.650
I need some help determining the size of
some potatoes.

1456
01:36:14.950 --> 01:36:15.310
Potatoes?

1457
01:36:15.610 --> 01:36:16.650
I think that's my without.

1458
01:36:16.850 --> 01:36:18.790
I think Metzger lied to me about a name.

1459
01:36:18.791 --> 01:36:22.390
Can you see if there's a connection
between Jean and someone named Sarah?

1460
01:36:23.150 --> 01:36:25.110
Hmm. his potatoes sound meager.

1461
01:36:27.230 --> 01:36:27.670
Oh. wow.

1462
01:36:27.770 --> 01:36:28.970
That really is your own place.

1463
01:36:29.430 --> 01:36:30.430
Well. well. well.

1464
01:36:30.830 --> 01:36:34.380
Internet. government records.
and a lot of data related

1465
01:36:34.381 --> 01:36:38.010
to Jean Grey has been
scrubbed by damage control.

1466
01:36:38.590 --> 01:36:39.590
They never what?

1467
01:36:40.250 --> 01:36:41.250
Her sister.

1468
01:36:42.090 --> 01:36:43.110
Wait. Jean has a sister.

1469
01:36:45.150 --> 01:36:45.370
Hmm.

1470
01:36:46.050 --> 01:36:47.050
Sarah Grey.

1471
01:36:47.730 --> 01:36:48.730
Also. a telepath.

1472
01:36:49.210 --> 01:36:52.730
Damage control took her into custody for
study and observation.

1473
01:36:53.430 --> 01:36:55.550
I mean. you can probably guess what they
mean by that.

1474
01:36:55.690 --> 01:36:57.570
Spearmitation and other human rights
violations?

1475
01:36:57.750 --> 01:36:58.750
Yes. exactly.

1476
01:36:58.790 --> 01:36:59.410
Wait. who are you?

1477
01:36:59.810 --> 01:37:01.150
Hi. that means...

1478
01:37:01.750 --> 01:37:02.750
Hi!

1479
01:37:02.950 --> 01:37:07.470
I'm sorry. I... I'm just so happy
that this sad man has friends.

1480
01:37:09.690 --> 01:37:10.690
Thanks.

1481
01:37:11.050 --> 01:37:12.070
I owe you one.

1482
01:37:13.290 --> 01:37:14.410
Good luck. Spider-Man.

1483
01:37:14.411 --> 01:37:15.411
Bye.

1484
01:37:15.890 --> 01:37:19.610
She was just looking for her sister. and
I handed her to the people who took her.

1485
01:37:19.890 --> 01:37:20.470
I gotta go.

1486
01:37:20.770 --> 01:37:21.770
Hey. Peter?

1487
01:37:21.810 --> 01:37:22.810
Yeah.

1488
01:37:23.510 --> 01:37:24.830
You should be careful. all right?

1489
01:37:26.690 --> 01:37:27.690
Yeah.

1490
01:37:32.590 --> 01:37:34.010
Spider-Man's name is Peter?

1491
01:37:49.070 --> 01:37:50.290
Jean. who do you want to be?

1492
01:37:52.990 --> 01:37:53.990
Her.

1493
01:37:54.110 --> 01:37:55.110
Pink jacket.

1494
01:37:56.310 --> 01:37:57.310
She's too far.

1495
01:37:58.510 --> 01:37:59.510
You gonna hop?

1496
01:38:01.190 --> 01:38:02.670
First. pick someone close.

1497
01:38:12.040 --> 01:38:13.080
And then...

1498
01:38:19.170 --> 01:38:21.690
Each hop has a limit. but...

1499
01:38:22.250 --> 01:38:24.410
you can string them together and go as far
as you want.

1500
01:38:25.090 --> 01:38:26.690
And when you let go...

1501
01:38:27.590 --> 01:38:29.030
you're right back where you started.

1502
01:38:30.270 --> 01:38:32.270
Could you do that to everyone in this park
at once?

1503
01:38:33.730 --> 01:38:34.730
Yeah. maybe one day.

1504
01:38:35.610 --> 01:38:36.610
You get really good.

1505
01:38:50.710 --> 01:38:51.810
Now could you just...

1506
01:38:53.410 --> 01:38:54.410
send us away?

1507
01:38:55.810 --> 01:38:57.090
She wasn't really a mom.

1508
01:38:59.450 --> 01:39:00.610
Not like that. anyway.

1509
01:39:00.750 --> 01:39:01.090
She was.

1510
01:39:01.730 --> 01:39:02.730
Before we changed.

1511
01:39:03.290 --> 01:39:04.537
Yeah. well. if that's
all it takes for you

1512
01:39:04.538 --> 01:39:05.730
to stop being a mom.
then you're not a mom.

1513
01:39:05.731 --> 01:39:08.790
What would you do if you had daughters
like us?

1514
01:39:09.690 --> 01:39:10.690
I'd love them.

1515
01:39:14.360 --> 01:39:15.360
Especially the redhead.

1516
01:39:15.420 --> 01:39:16.420
Shut up.

1517
01:39:18.400 --> 01:39:19.480
We have each other.

1518
01:39:21.500 --> 01:39:24.440
You think we have ice cream?

1519
01:39:27.060 --> 01:39:28.060
On the chip or chocolate?

1520
01:40:52.920 --> 01:40:54.040
Subject is awake.

1521
01:40:54.041 --> 01:40:56.180
Heart rate is 94 BPM.

1522
01:40:58.940 --> 01:41:00.500
Jean. that's not going to work anymore.

1523
01:41:01.000 --> 01:41:02.000
Thanks to Spiderman.

1524
01:41:05.760 --> 01:41:06.760
Jean.

1525
01:41:15.040 --> 01:41:16.480
I need you to breathe.

1526
01:41:17.100 --> 01:41:18.580
I need you to look at me and breathe.

1527
01:41:19.160 --> 01:41:20.160
Okay?

1528
01:41:20.280 --> 01:41:21.280
You're safe.

1529
01:41:21.440 --> 01:41:22.440
Breathe.

1530
01:41:24.060 --> 01:41:25.060
Where is she?

1531
01:41:26.900 --> 01:41:28.978
Like your sister. you've
been blessed with a power that

1532
01:41:28.979 --> 01:41:31.220
has the potential to do
tremendous good in the world.

1533
01:41:32.280 --> 01:41:33.280
Or tremendous damage.

1534
01:41:34.140 --> 01:41:37.960
The power like yours in the hands of a
child is an impossible burden.

1535
01:41:40.020 --> 01:41:40.980
But imagine...

1536
01:41:40.981 --> 01:41:45.441
if that power was placed in the hands of
people who actually know what to do with it.

1537
01:41:53.300 --> 01:41:54.700
Where is my sister?

1538
01:41:54.701 --> 01:41:59.560
You're going to change the world.
Jean.

1539
01:42:00.260 --> 01:42:01.260
Hey!

1540
01:42:01.920 --> 01:42:02.920
Hey!

1541
01:42:04.620 --> 01:42:05.620
Go!

1542
01:42:28.530 --> 01:42:30.630
You've got eyes everywhere. kid.

1543
01:42:32.190 --> 01:42:34.730
Look. Frank. everything's all kidnapped
Jean's sister.

1544
01:42:34.910 --> 01:42:36.226
Jean was just trying to find her.

1545
01:42:36.250 --> 01:42:37.490
We were wrong about everything.

1546
01:42:37.670 --> 01:42:39.210
It's sentimental horse shit.

1547
01:42:40.270 --> 01:42:42.570
You see what she can do and what she's
capable of.

1548
01:42:42.610 --> 01:42:44.006
What. you're going to let her loose?

1549
01:42:44.030 --> 01:42:45.310
Is that what you're going to do?

1550
01:42:45.930 --> 01:42:47.830
I can tell you right now. you do that.

1551
01:42:49.010 --> 01:42:50.210
I ain't going to run my way.

1552
01:42:50.950 --> 01:42:52.330
Frank. please get out of here.

1553
01:42:52.730 --> 01:42:53.730
Frank!

1554
01:43:07.400 --> 01:43:08.400
This is Joe.

1555
01:43:08.860 --> 01:43:10.100
Forty foot clearance.

1556
01:43:10.460 --> 01:43:11.460
Lock and down the room.

1557
01:43:11.940 --> 01:43:12.940
Lock and down.

1558
01:43:18.450 --> 01:43:19.450
Disengage inevitable.

1559
01:43:24.100 --> 01:43:26.120
Change of power is enough for the
operation.

1560
01:43:36.380 --> 01:43:39.180
As you can tell. we're beyond your jump
rates.

1561
01:43:41.420 --> 01:43:42.920
Tell me what VMAX is.

1562
01:43:43.880 --> 01:43:45.720
You're the second person to ask me about
that.

1563
01:43:45.960 --> 01:43:48.300
I have no idea what that means.

1564
01:43:48.640 --> 01:43:49.920
She sent me a message.

1565
01:43:50.980 --> 01:43:52.460
She was trying to help me find her.

1566
01:43:53.680 --> 01:43:57.240
She communicated with you telepathically
across all that distance.

1567
01:43:58.100 --> 01:44:00.940
We did register a huge spike in that
session.

1568
01:44:03.500 --> 01:44:04.500
Fascinating.

1569
01:44:04.700 --> 01:44:06.260
What does it mean. asshole?

1570
01:44:08.380 --> 01:44:09.380
I don't know.

1571
01:44:10.580 --> 01:44:11.580
Let's begin.

1572
01:44:20.540 --> 01:44:23.020
I work with Sarah Stenchen on two areas.

1573
01:44:23.880 --> 01:44:28.740
Identifying the source of her power and
identifying her path towards copying it.

1574
01:44:29.380 --> 01:44:33.460
If we could find a way to record a
telepathic brain during a jump.

1575
01:44:33.461 --> 01:44:38.540
then perhaps we could replicate those
pathways in the mind of our choosing.

1576
01:44:40.100 --> 01:44:43.120
This instrument is your sister's legacy.

1577
01:44:44.340 --> 01:44:47.060
We build this together over many months of
trial and error.

1578
01:44:48.600 --> 01:44:50.240
I hope you and I can honor her sacrifice.

1579
01:44:53.420 --> 01:44:54.740
What are you talking about?

1580
01:44:56.660 --> 01:44:57.660
Trigger the first jump.

1581
01:45:02.500 --> 01:45:04.620
Tell me what VMAX is.

1582
01:45:05.180 --> 01:45:06.700
I know that's where you're hiding her.

1583
01:45:21.660 --> 01:45:22.660
She's jumping.

1584
01:45:24.980 --> 01:45:25.980
Coffee.

1585
01:45:26.400 --> 01:45:27.400
We're in full lockdown.

1586
01:45:27.940 --> 01:45:28.980
The process has commenced.

1587
01:45:29.480 --> 01:45:30.480
What process?

1588
01:45:31.640 --> 01:45:33.700
Hey. whoa. that's a pretty serious look
there. dude.

1589
01:45:34.980 --> 01:45:36.280
Hey. whoa. what the hell. man?

1590
01:45:36.400 --> 01:45:37.516
Come on. I'm afraid of damage.

1591
01:45:37.540 --> 01:45:38.660
Control. what are you doing?

1592
01:45:42.620 --> 01:45:44.480
Huh. it's gonna be like that if you wanna
go.

1593
01:45:45.280 --> 01:45:47.340
Alright. alright. just give me a sec.

1594
01:45:48.220 --> 01:45:49.220
Give me a sec.

1595
01:45:49.820 --> 01:45:51.240
I'm not in high school anymore.

1596
01:45:53.340 --> 01:45:54.180
Did you stretch?

1597
01:45:54.340 --> 01:45:54.880
Are you a big stretcher?

1598
01:45:55.320 --> 01:45:55.960
I mean. you should do it.

1599
01:45:56.020 --> 01:45:57.020
You're a lot of work.

1600
01:45:57.320 --> 01:45:57.800
What about you?

1601
01:45:57.820 --> 01:45:58.820
Are you guys stretched?

1602
01:45:59.000 --> 01:46:00.180
It's so good for you.

1603
01:46:01.960 --> 01:46:02.960
You ready?

1604
01:46:32.660 --> 01:46:33.860
Where is Jean Grey?

1605
01:46:36.020 --> 01:46:37.020
This is jump 26.

1606
01:46:37.560 --> 01:46:38.560
Recordings look good.

1607
01:46:38.840 --> 01:46:39.840
Excuse me. sir.

1608
01:46:40.700 --> 01:46:41.700
We have an entry.

1609
01:46:46.560 --> 01:46:47.560
You were right.

1610
01:46:48.440 --> 01:46:49.800
She's much stronger than a sister.

1611
01:46:50.960 --> 01:46:52.020
Increase the frequency.

1612
01:46:53.460 --> 01:46:55.000
You're doing very well. Jean.

1613
01:47:40.620 --> 01:47:42.020
Jean?

1614
01:47:46.540 --> 01:47:48.440
Jean. can you hear me?

1615
01:47:54.260 --> 01:47:55.260
Jean?

1616
01:47:58.900 --> 01:48:00.600
You're a murderer.

1617
01:48:03.460 --> 01:48:05.580
Her frequencies are evolving.

1618
01:48:06.600 --> 01:48:07.600
This doesn't make sense.

1619
01:48:08.240 --> 01:48:12.400
The last thing my sister saw was this
room.

1620
01:48:13.040 --> 01:48:16.300
The brain waves are somehow affecting the
object. so I'm gonna shut it down.

1621
01:48:16.880 --> 01:48:17.500
I'm trying. sir.

1622
01:48:17.780 --> 01:48:19.020
What do you mean you're trying?

1623
01:48:19.120 --> 01:48:23.700
The last thing my sister saw was this
goddamn room!

1624
01:48:24.260 --> 01:48:25.020
Shut it down!

1625
01:48:25.260 --> 01:48:26.260
I can't. sir.

1626
01:48:29.700 --> 01:48:31.960
I can't let you do that. Bill.

1627
01:48:35.420 --> 01:48:41.440
The only hands that will wield this power
are mine.

1628
01:50:50.370 --> 01:50:51.430
What do you want?

1629
01:50:56.170 --> 01:50:57.930
Jean. I'm here to help you.

1630
01:50:59.370 --> 01:51:00.470
You put me here.

1631
01:51:01.430 --> 01:51:05.110
I know. and I'm sorry about Sarah.
and I'm sorry that I got it so wrong.

1632
01:51:07.550 --> 01:51:11.390
If you came here to save a helpless girl
from damage control. you're too late.

1633
01:51:12.550 --> 01:51:13.870
They're the ones who need saving.

1634
01:51:14.230 --> 01:51:17.450
And now. so are you.

1635
01:51:19.230 --> 01:51:20.830
Here we go.

1636
01:51:28.630 --> 01:51:36.160
God. that's cool.

1637
01:51:37.820 --> 01:51:58.450
Get in. please!

1638
01:52:18.290 --> 01:52:19.290
Fuck!

1639
01:52:35.400 --> 01:52:42.520
Isn't it funny how your friends from
damage control developed a special...

1640
01:52:42.521 --> 01:52:44.480
They've got a whole task force ready.

1641
01:52:45.240 --> 01:52:46.800
Just in case you ever get out of line.

1642
01:52:51.200 --> 01:52:52.420
People are monsters.

1643
01:52:58.490 --> 01:53:00.190
Any more than they trust you.

1644
01:53:01.930 --> 01:53:02.930
Frank.

1645
01:53:14.630 --> 01:53:15.630
Good phone. kid.

1646
01:53:16.110 --> 01:53:18.390
Just gotta hold everyone within a
kilometer of the island.

1647
01:53:19.250 --> 01:53:20.250
Wait. what?

1648
01:53:26.040 --> 01:53:28.480
Look. if you're gonna do something.
you better do it now.

1649
01:54:08.280 --> 01:54:09.320
Damn it.

1650
01:54:33.040 --> 01:54:36.320
My sister died in this room.

1651
01:54:37.820 --> 01:54:39.080
Surrounded by these men.

1652
01:54:40.500 --> 01:54:43.100
And her only crime was that she was
special.

1653
01:54:44.960 --> 01:54:46.100
Just like you.

1654
01:54:48.000 --> 01:54:49.000
Just like me.

1655
01:54:51.700 --> 01:54:54.740
People like us don't get to live a normal
life.

1656
01:54:57.540 --> 01:54:59.220
We don't get to have friends.

1657
01:55:00.140 --> 01:55:01.140
Or a family.

1658
01:55:03.240 --> 01:55:04.400
Those people are gone.

1659
01:55:07.400 --> 01:55:09.040
That life is over.

1660
01:55:35.780 --> 01:55:37.960
So why don't you just be honest with
yourself?

1661
01:55:41.340 --> 01:55:42.440
Are you Peter Parker?

1662
01:55:44.680 --> 01:55:46.100
Or are you Spider-Man?

1663
01:56:19.960 --> 01:56:20.960
I'm both.

1664
01:58:08.650 --> 01:58:10.130
Jean. please.

1665
01:58:12.090 --> 01:58:13.330
This won't make it right.

1666
01:58:15.750 --> 01:58:17.590
Come on. you're not a killer. Jean.

1667
01:58:17.790 --> 01:58:18.870
You have no idea what I am.

1668
01:58:20.810 --> 01:58:22.430
I know that you loved your sister.

1669
01:58:26.160 --> 01:58:28.680
And I know that losing her felt like he
lost everything.

1670
01:58:29.300 --> 01:58:31.060
If you come any closer. he dies!

1671
01:58:31.400 --> 01:58:32.400
They hold you!

1672
01:58:50.910 --> 01:58:52.750
You know this won't bring her back.
right Jean?

1673
01:59:10.910 --> 01:59:12.950
Don't be so sure I can't get into your
mind.

1674
01:59:15.170 --> 01:59:17.350
I'm a lot more powerful since I last
tried.

1675
01:59:37.910 --> 01:59:38.910
Hey.

1676
01:59:40.470 --> 01:59:41.470
Hey.

1677
01:59:43.890 --> 01:59:47.930
I think you don't have to listen to me and
I've got powers.

1678
01:59:52.050 --> 01:59:58.890
You know. this whole thing can get really
scary.

1679
02:00:00.030 --> 02:00:01.030
You know that?

1680
02:00:19.790 --> 02:00:21.230
It's already pretty scary.

1681
02:00:22.910 --> 02:00:23.390
Yeah.

1682
02:00:23.391 --> 02:00:27.230
And things can change very quickly.

1683
02:00:28.230 --> 02:00:30.670
Ways that we can't even imagine right now.

1684
02:00:31.230 --> 02:00:32.230
I know.

1685
02:00:32.370 --> 02:00:32.670
No.

1686
02:00:33.310 --> 02:00:37.530
I don't think you do know.

1687
02:00:39.610 --> 02:00:40.610
What do you mean?

1688
02:00:44.560 --> 02:00:46.200
You're a really special person.

1689
02:00:48.060 --> 02:00:51.500
And I would hope that that will always
make you feel really great about yourself.

1690
02:00:52.460 --> 02:00:54.760
But I know sometimes it doesn't.

1691
02:00:55.620 --> 02:00:57.920
Sometimes it'll be really lonely.

1692
02:01:04.260 --> 02:01:13.261
And sometimes. because you're special.
people can do dark. monstrous things to you.

1693
02:01:14.880 --> 02:01:18.880
But. this is what I want you to know.

1694
02:01:21.000 --> 02:01:22.000
You're beautiful.

1695
02:01:23.220 --> 02:01:25.620
And the people who love you. we love you.

1696
02:01:25.900 --> 02:01:27.640
Not because you're special. we love you.

1697
02:01:27.660 --> 02:01:28.660
But because you're you.

1698
02:01:31.000 --> 02:01:33.000
I want you to remember that.

1699
02:01:35.000 --> 02:01:36.880
Even when it feels like you're totally
alone.

1700
02:01:40.000 --> 02:01:41.860
That's your deepest responsibility.

1701
02:01:45.620 --> 02:01:48.900
Never forget that. no matter how
powerfully they come.

1702
02:02:23.500 --> 02:02:25.140
I'm sorry about your sister.

1703
02:02:30.900 --> 02:02:32.000
I'm sorry about your aunt.

1704
02:02:36.280 --> 02:02:37.620
Yeah. you would have loved her.

1705
02:02:41.510 --> 02:02:43.310
Just because we've lost someone.

1706
02:02:46.810 --> 02:02:48.850
It doesn't mean we have to do this alone.

1707
02:02:51.450 --> 02:02:53.570
I mean. we can.

1708
02:02:54.390 --> 02:02:55.050
Trust me. I'm sorry.

1709
02:02:55.051 --> 02:02:56.051
We have been trying.

1710
02:02:59.650 --> 02:03:00.650
It doesn't work.

1711
02:03:05.940 --> 02:03:06.940
Even if that's true.

1712
02:03:11.500 --> 02:03:12.740
I have no one.

1713
02:03:17.560 --> 02:03:18.600
You have me?

1714
02:04:02.260 --> 02:04:03.260
You are?

1715
02:04:04.340 --> 02:04:05.340
Fine.

1716
02:04:10.340 --> 02:04:11.340
I'm okay.

1717
02:04:13.000 --> 02:04:14.136
I'm okay. I'm okay. I'm okay.

1718
02:04:14.160 --> 02:04:15.160
Peter!

1719
02:04:18.980 --> 02:04:19.320
Peter!

1720
02:04:19.800 --> 02:04:19.800
Peter!

1721
02:04:20.640 --> 02:04:22.000
No. no. no. Peter!

1722
02:04:23.800 --> 02:04:25.100
You gotta get out of here.

1723
02:04:25.400 --> 02:04:26.400
Don't be looking for me.

1724
02:04:26.440 --> 02:04:27.200
No. no. no. no. no.

1725
02:04:27.220 --> 02:04:28.160
Please just stay with me.

1726
02:04:28.220 --> 02:04:29.580
Come on. hold on. come on. please!

1727
02:04:29.980 --> 02:04:30.980
Peter!

1728
02:04:31.200 --> 02:04:32.200
Peter!

1729
02:04:33.720 --> 02:04:34.720
Just go.

1730
02:04:35.920 --> 02:04:36.260
Peter!

1731
02:04:36.920 --> 02:04:37.920
Look at me.

1732
02:04:56.040 --> 02:04:59.540
A Spider-Man arrived at Bellevue Hospital
with a bullet wound.

1733
02:05:00.220 --> 02:05:01.280
Seemingly a death story.

1734
02:05:03.860 --> 02:05:06.273
The reclusive crime
fighter is in critical condition

1735
02:05:06.274 --> 02:05:09.220
as the city's top medical
experts work to save him.

1736
02:05:12.380 --> 02:05:15.100
Tonight. all eyes are on Spider-Man.

1737
02:05:16.820 --> 02:05:19.583
The hero who saved
New York so many times is

1738
02:05:19.584 --> 02:05:22.801
now in the hands of
its best and brightest.

1739
02:05:24.000 --> 02:06:28.840
And the people of New
York hold their breath.

1740
02:06:36.450 --> 02:06:41.150
No. no. no. no. no. hey.

1741
02:06:41.350 --> 02:06:42.350
Where's my mask?

1742
02:06:42.550 --> 02:06:44.070
Someone left there. I got you covered.

1743
02:06:44.250 --> 02:06:45.250
You're good.

1744
02:06:45.370 --> 02:06:45.830
Where is she?

1745
02:06:45.950 --> 02:06:46.490
Is she okay?

1746
02:06:46.810 --> 02:06:47.810
Yeah. she's okay.

1747
02:06:47.910 --> 02:06:48.910
She's okay.

1748
02:06:48.970 --> 02:06:49.970
Where is she?

1749
02:06:51.250 --> 02:06:52.590
I think maybe she just left.

1750
02:06:54.310 --> 02:06:59.070
She was using her magic voodoo shit to
keep you alive.

1751
02:07:01.630 --> 02:07:02.930
Yeah. she's alright.

1752
02:07:10.360 --> 02:07:11.360
I'm sorry.

1753
02:07:16.350 --> 02:07:16.590
Frank.

1754
02:07:16.690 --> 02:07:19.550
Just. just. I'm really sorry for what I
did.

1755
02:07:19.710 --> 02:07:20.130
No. Frank.

1756
02:07:20.150 --> 02:07:23.230
I know there's a lot of things.
but it sure shit ain't okay. alright?

1757
02:07:27.340 --> 02:07:28.340
I see.

1758
02:07:30.080 --> 02:07:31.540
I see real bravery.

1759
02:07:31.541 --> 02:07:33.960
I see that you killed my day.

1760
02:07:35.940 --> 02:07:36.940
But that happened.

1761
02:07:38.540 --> 02:07:39.580
That was something else.

1762
02:07:43.040 --> 02:07:44.040
You crying?

1763
02:07:44.700 --> 02:07:46.360
No. I ain't crying.

1764
02:07:50.360 --> 02:07:55.700
No. you look exactly where I thought you
would.

1765
02:07:57.440 --> 02:07:59.020
A nice kid.

1766
02:07:59.021 --> 02:08:00.021
I did.

1767
02:08:01.800 --> 02:08:03.240
Never had a friend like that.

1768
02:08:05.280 --> 02:08:06.340
Only friends now.

1769
02:08:14.240 --> 02:08:15.820
I can't believe I just saw you cry.

1770
02:08:16.120 --> 02:08:18.560
I didn't cry like I'm talking about it.

1771
02:08:18.600 --> 02:08:19.600
Bullshit.

1772
02:08:21.480 --> 02:08:22.480
Oh. yeah.

1773
02:08:23.100 --> 02:08:24.500
I've been doing it all night.

1774
02:08:25.340 --> 02:08:26.700
Been here since you walked in.

1775
02:08:26.920 --> 02:08:27.920
Just take a look.

1776
02:08:38.950 --> 02:08:39.950
Yo. kid.

1777
02:08:40.290 --> 02:08:42.010
You came in there to cut through the suit.

1778
02:08:42.410 --> 02:08:46.370
But when you're ready to split.
I got a plan.

1779
02:09:01.780 --> 02:09:02.780
Hey!

1780
02:09:10.220 --> 02:09:11.380
It's Spider-Man!

1781
02:11:45.600 --> 02:11:51.010
I've been thinking a lot about what you
said.

1782
02:11:53.830 --> 02:11:57.267
And you'd be happy to
know that I've decided I'm

1783
02:11:57.268 --> 02:12:00.030
not... I'm not going to
do this alone anymore.

1784
02:12:09.770 --> 02:12:10.770
Don't miss you. mate.

1785
02:12:19.260 --> 02:12:22.235
I mean. I still got a little
pain in my back. but I could

1786
02:12:22.236 --> 02:12:24.621
probably get back out there
if you need me for a minute.

1787
02:12:24.680 --> 02:12:26.500
But what I need you to do is rest.

1788
02:12:27.120 --> 02:12:27.800
I know. I know.

1789
02:12:27.960 --> 02:12:29.356
But come on. you got to give me something.

1790
02:12:29.380 --> 02:12:30.900
I mean. how's the investigation going?

1791
02:12:31.240 --> 02:12:33.460
Well. Mexico's still missing.

1792
02:12:34.360 --> 02:12:37.840
But your friend. Black Widow. she's been
helping us.

1793
02:12:38.040 --> 02:12:39.260
They do all the records.

1794
02:12:39.740 --> 02:12:41.900
Damage control tried to have scrubbed.

1795
02:12:42.140 --> 02:12:44.280
Had me drop by her office. the other day.

1796
02:12:44.600 --> 02:12:45.600
And how was that?

1797
02:12:46.260 --> 02:12:48.340
Well. uh. my skin feels amazing.

1798
02:12:50.440 --> 02:12:51.100
Attention all units.

1799
02:12:51.340 --> 02:12:53.100
We have a confirmed bank robbery in
progress.

1800
02:12:53.640 --> 02:12:54.680
Hey. are you getting this?

1801
02:12:56.500 --> 02:12:57.200
Yeah. I'm on it.

1802
02:12:57.480 --> 02:12:58.460
Hey. it's not that hard for me.

1803
02:12:58.480 --> 02:12:59.720
I could probably meet you down.

1804
02:12:59.940 --> 02:13:01.940
No. we can handle a robbery.

1805
02:13:03.120 --> 02:13:05.580
Just try to take care of yourself.

1806
02:13:07.840 --> 02:13:08.840
Okay.

1807
02:13:09.840 --> 02:13:10.840
You too.

1808
02:13:11.400 --> 02:13:12.700
Say hello to E.J.

1809
02:13:12.920 --> 02:13:14.040
Marley for me.

1810
02:13:14.800 --> 02:13:15.800
Okay.

1811
02:13:17.800 --> 02:13:19.220
Spiderman says hello.

1812
02:13:55.300 --> 02:13:56.300
Hi.

1813
02:13:56.860 --> 02:13:57.860
Uh. hey.

1814
02:14:00.100 --> 02:14:02.600
Oh. uh. flower guy. right?

1815
02:14:02.900 --> 02:14:03.900
From the party?

1816
02:14:05.120 --> 02:14:06.120
I'm Peter.

1817
02:14:07.580 --> 02:14:08.580
Okay. hello.

1818
02:14:09.680 --> 02:14:30.580
SUBS: CRETA STAR

